### Tiny rails
| Case | emit-c rc / s / RSS KB | check rc / s / RSS KB | Note |
|------|-----------------------:|----------------------:|------|
| `println(tok)` bare | 1 / 0.01 / 4408 | 1 / 0.02 / 5172 | dual refuse |
| `println((1), tok)` | 1 / 0.02 / 4764 | **0** / 0.01 / 5224 | check **FN** |
| `println(("x") + tok)` | **0** / 0.02 / 5048 | **0** / 0.01 / 5288 | emit **leak** |
| `eprintln((1), tok)` | 1 / 0.02 / 4892 | **0** / 0.01 / 5364 | guard; check FN |
| `eprintln(("x") + tok)` | 1 / 0.03 / 5084 | **0** / 0.01 / 5476 | guard; check FN |
| public `println(1)` | 0 / 0.01 / 4572 | 0 / 0.01 / 4796 | no secret |

Grouped emit-c **tracks** bare / eprintln (~4.4–5.1 MB). Check on the
hole is the public-check class (~5.2 MB) because it **FNs**. No extra
join on the stmt rail.

### Nested `println( (^{d} 1 )^{d} , tok)`
| d | src B | emit-c s / RSS | check s / RSS |
|--:|------:|---------------:|--------------:|
| 1 | 80 | 0.02 / 4792 | 0.01 / 5424 |
| 8 | 94 | 0.02 / 5128 | 0.02 / 5960 |
| 32 | 142 | 0.02 / 5944 | 0.04 / 7796 |
| 64 | 206 | 0.04 / 6640 | 0.06 / 10228 |
| 128 | 334 | 0.05 / 8896 | 0.12 / 15164 |

64→128 check ≈ **1.48×** RSS for 2× depth. Same class as s29b
(1.47×). A walk concat bomb would be tens–hundreds of MB at d=128.
This ELF **does not run** the Int walk (check FN → typecheck nest).

